{
  "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
  "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:31 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Stephen I. Vladeck",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When this case was first argued to this Court two years ago, counsel for Respondent and counsel for the United States were both asked whether Petitioners would have a Bivens remedy if Sergio Hernandez had been standing on U.S. soil when he was shot and killed by Respondent. Both said yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: -- just to go with the first of the things you mentioned, the international relations, there has been diplomatic correspondence between the Mexican government and our government with respect to this -- this -- this incident."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Border Patrol has conducted an investigation, and it reached the determination that the action of the agent was not contrary to policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. VLADECK",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. VLADECK: So I do -- I certainly agree that the -- that the country is supposed to speak with one voice, Mr. Chief Justice. Two -- two points in response. The first is, of course, if the government continues to believe and if Respondent continues to believe there would be a Bivens remedy if Sergio Hernandez had simply been standing on American soil, it's not clear to me why the same concerns wouldn't be equally present."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: They argue it's not merely the foreign policy implications that the Chief Justice identified but that border security is also national security in some respects and that that's a different context, slightly different than the foreign relations. Can you address that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. VLADECK",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "reason why we believe this is in the heartland of Bivens, notwithstanding the concerns that the Chief Justice has referred to and that Justice Kavanaugh alluded to, is because, here, we do not have a case where the claim is that a particular policy of the United States in the foreign relations or national security sphere was the source of the injury to the plaintiffs. Here, our argument is that the policy is actually coextensive with the Constitution, and so that if we are correct, which we have not yet, of course, had a chance to prove, but if we are correct that Respondent violated Petitioner's constitutional -- or Sergio Hernandez's constitutional rights, Justice Alito, there would also be a violation of policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: If we can go back to the -- this complaint, and at this stage, this very preliminary stage, we're supposed to accept the complaint's allegations as true, which is that, here, we have a rogue officer acting in violation of the agency's own instruction, using excessive force to kill a child at play, how does that call into question any foreign policy or national security policy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why? What's the greater instability when you already admit that Bivens -- Bivens would apply if that child was standing two feet from the border? And it even would apply, according to you, if it was an American child standing two feet on the Mexican border. I don't see where the greater instability arises in that situation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ortega",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Fourth Amendment, I believe, is foreclosed by Verdugo in its language claiming that a U.S. agent, even acting on foreign soil, is not constrained by the Fourth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But do you agree there could be serious foreign policy implications even from a incident inside the United States with a victim who's a Mexican national?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ortega",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the myriad of special factors, including the separation of powers, national security, foreign diplomacy, public policy, and the projected costs, I think that that creates quite a different -- a different picture of that. And it's better left for Congress and the executive to decide those issues and, specifically, Congress to balance the public policy"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why -- why chaos?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ortega",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The lower courts have stood on this Court's presumption against the extension in order to provide stability and guidance to them in their decisions. Extending it again and extending it transnationally would create a myriad of problems."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ortega",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the border is real. It's a real line. And it can't be extended. The Constitution cannot be extended into a foreign country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey B. Wall",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A foreign national was killed on foreign soil by a federal officer patrolling an international border. That is plainly a new context for Bivens purposes, and several special factors counsel hesitation here: clear foreign relations concerns with Mexico and the need for border security, clear extraterritoriality, and clear signals from Congress in 1983 and the FTCA that it does not approve of damages liability for injuries abroad."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey B. Wall",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0002-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "happy to go through all the reports and the evidence. I'm happy to say, look, there were 55 incidents of use of force with firearms in fiscal year '12. There were 15 last year in fiscal year '18. That's a more than 70 percent drop."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Did you say you disagree, Mr. Wall?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So the three inches inside the line, what would be the -- the case there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: And how about 10 miles"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6c33ad8f915221ed07d0d21e68806a164ac525a0de14869477c92d586a68117d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6c33ad8f9152-0003-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. VLADECK: So, Justice Ginsburg, that goes again to the question of whether extraterritoriality is a special factor counseling hesitation. And I want to be clear, we agree that there will be much harder cases, if, say, for example, Agent Mesa was miles into Mexico, somehow acting under legal authority. But RJR Nabisco reinforces, it does not distinguish Kiobel in its suggestion that the presumption against extraterritoriality -- Mr. Chief Justice -- can be displaced when the underlying conduct touches and concerns U.S. territory with sufficient force to displace the presumption."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1678",
      "confidence": 0.0,
